\title{topicsovertime: Topics over Time: A Continuous-Time Topic Model}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Fits the Topics over Time model of Wang and McCallum (2006) \doi{10.1145/1150402.1150450}, a latent Dirichlet allocation style topic model in which each topic also has a Beta distribution over continuous time, so topics are shaped by both word co-occurrence and document timestamps without discretizing time or assuming Markov dynamics. Inference uses collapsed Gibbs sampling implemented in 'C++'. Includes prediction of topic proportions and timestamps for new documents, topic trends over time, and simulation of synthetic corpora.
